 Periods: `start` and `end` are ISO-8601 UTC strings on the hour. A period of a day or more is made of whole
 days, both at midnight, and `end` is the start of the day after the last rented day. `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or an invalid period, and
-`book` throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period. Cancellations (with the 24-hour
-no-refund policy) are not implemented yet.
+`book` throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period.
+
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` — cancels the booking at `at` (an ISO-8601 UTC string) and returns
+  `{ bookingId, refund }`, in euro cents. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, so it is free
+  again for `book` and `availability`. The refund is the full total when `at` is at least 24 hours before
+  the booking's start, and nothing when it is less (including after the start). It throws for an unknown
+  booking, an already cancelled booking or an invalid `at`.
